  "note": [
    "Kulish (1905, ebible ukr1871) verses pasted by script from the gracious-tech/fetch_collection ukr_pan USFM mirror (scripts/bible_mirror.py ukr_pan); U+201F normalised to “. A row is mined only when the translator reported it verbatim AND the normalised Kulish text (marks and punctuation aside, 12+ characters) is found in that block; adapted, joined-with-ellipsis and self-rendered quotations are self_rendered.",
    "Murray's Roman-numeral citations (Jas. iv. 2) are printed with Arabic numerals and Kulish book names (Якова 4:2); Hebrews as Євреїв (library majority). Two citation slips were repaired in every edition in this PR: Acts 1:14 (printed i. 13) and Jeremiah 17:14 (printed xii. 14).",
    "Where Kulish cannot carry Murray's wording, Kulish is quoted and the point left to Murray's prose: Mark 11:24 «одержите» (future) for 'have received' (the numbered fragments in ch. 11 adapt it to «одержали», following school-of-prayer.uk — self_rendered); Zechariah 12:10 «духа ласки й побожностї» has no 'supplication', so the title and prose use «Дух благання»; Habakkuk 3:2 «доверши твоє дїло» (complete) for 'revive'; Job 15:4 has no 'restrainest prayer'; Isaiah 59:16 «дивився» for 'wondered'; Romans 8:27 «промовляє» for 'maketh intercession'.",
    "AI-translated (job #7450) by six translators against one pinned conventions file; tag sequence identical to the English per chapter; awaiting native review."
